.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt THR_KILL 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm thr_kill ,
.Nm thr_kill2 ,
.Nm thr_sigqueueinfo
.Nd send signal to thread
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/thr.h
.Ft int
.Fn thr_kill "long id" "int sig"
.Ft int
.Fn thr_kill2 "pid_t pid" "long id" "int sig"
.Ft int
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo "pid_t pid" "long id" "int sig" "const siginfo_t *info"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn thr_kill
and
.Fn thr_kill2
system calls allow sending a signal, specified by the
.Fa sig
argument, to some threads in a process.
For the
.Fn thr_kill
function, signalled threads are always limited to the current process.
For the
.Fn thr_kill2
function, the
.Fa pid
argument specifies the process with threads to be signalled.
.Pp
The
.Fa id
argument specifies which threads get the signal.
If
.Fa id
is equal to \-1, all threads in the specified process are signalled.
Otherwise, only the thread with the thread identifier equal to the
argument is signalled.
.Pp
The
.Fa sig
argument defines the delivered signal.
It must be a valid signal number or zero.
In the latter case no signal is actually sent, and the call is used to
verify the liveness of the thread.
.Pp
The signal is delivered with
.Dv siginfo
.Dv si_code
set to
.Dv SI_LWP .
.Pp
The
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
system call queues the signal
.Fa sig
to the thread with the identifier
.Fa id
in the process
.Fa pid ,
with the signal information that
.Fa info
points to.
The
.Va si_signo
member is set to
.Fa sig .
If
.Fa pid
is the current process, the other members are delivered as they are,
whatever the value of
.Va si_code .
A process can use this to send again a signal that it caught, with the
original signal information.
If
.Fa pid
is another process,
.Va si_code
must be
.Dv SI_QUEUE ,
only
.Va si_value
is taken from
.Fa info ,
and
.Va si_pid
and
.Va si_uid
are set to the process identifier and the real user identifier of the
caller, as for
.Xr sigqueue 2 .
The signal is queued as by
.Xr sigqueue 2 ,
and the limit on the number of queued signals of the process applies.
A
.Fa sig
of zero only checks the existence of the thread and the permission.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If successful,
.Fn thr_kill ,
.Fn thr_kill2
and
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
will return zero, otherwise \-1 is returned, and
.Va errno
is set to indicate the error.
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn thr_kill ,
.Fn thr_kill2
and
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
operations return the following errors:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The
.Fa sig
argument is not zero and does not specify valid signal.
.It Bq Er ESRCH
The specified process or thread was not found.
.El
.Pp
Additionally, the
.Fn thr_kill2
and
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
may return the following errors:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EPERM
The current process does not have sufficient privilege to check existence or
send a signal to the specified process.
.El
.Pp
Additionally, the
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
may return the following errors:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The
.Fa pid
or the
.Fa id
argument is zero or negative.
.It Bq Er EPERM
The specified process is not the current process, and
.Va si_code
is not
.Dv SI_QUEUE .
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The
.Fa info
argument points outside the process address space.
.It Bq Er ECAPMODE
The current process is in capability mode, and the specified process is
not the current process.
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
The process has reached the limit on the number of queued signals.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr _umtx_op 2 ,
.Xr kill 2 ,
.Xr sigqueue 2 ,
.Xr thr_exit 2 ,
.Xr thr_new 2 ,
.Xr thr_self 2 ,
.Xr thr_set_name 2 ,
.Xr pthread_kill 3 ,
.Xr signal 3
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn thr_kill
and
.Fn thr_kill2
system calls are non-standard and are used by the
.Lb libthr
to implement
.St -p1003.1-2001
.Xr pthread 3
functionality.
The
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
system call is non-standard.
It gives the behavior of the Linux
.Fn rt_tgsigqueueinfo
system call.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn thr_kill
and
.Fn thr_kill2
system calls first appeared in
.Fx 5.2 .
The
.Fn thr_sigqueueinfo
system call first appeared in the freebsd-android-native fork of
.Fx 15.1 .
